2. The figures for the corresponding periods have been regrouped/reclassifed wherever consdiered necessary to confirm the figures represented in the current period. &lt;BR&gt; 
3. The activities of the Company releate to two segments - Dairy &amp; Kitchen Equipment and Defence Product &lt;BR&gt; 
4.The Company has acquired additional 2500 equity shares at a price of 19,000 each of waveoptix defence solutions private limited (WDSPL) on account of conversion of loan given amounting to Rs. 475 Lakhs as on 25th March, 2025. On such acqusition the company has investment of 40% equity share capital of WDSPL. &lt;BR&gt; 
5.The Company has acquired 88000 equity shares of 200 each of conceptia software technologies private limited (CSTPL) on 5th May, 2025 which represent 20% of equity CSTPL. On such acquisition CSTPL has become  associate of the company w.e.f. 05 May, 2025. &lt;BR&gt; 
6.The Company has issued 860000 convertible equity warrants at the price of rs.304 on 1st February 2024 on prefrential basis. The upfront 25% of the total considertaion was received at the time of subscribing warrants. &lt;BR&gt; 
The company has converted the 860000 convertible equity warrants into equity shares by receving the balance 75% of the total considertaion. The company had converted 541000 Convertible Equity warrants into Equity Shares as on 26th June, 2025 &amp; 3,19,000 Convertible Equity warrants into Equity Shares as on 25th July, 2025 by receiving the balance 75% of the total consideration. &lt;BR&gt; 
The company had received proceeds of Rs. 1960.80 Lakhs from the above issue., the company had utilized the above amount for meeting its working capital requirement and for Capital Expenditure requirement as per the objects mentioned in the Extra ordinary General Meeting Notice dated on 13th December, 2023. &lt;BR&gt; 
7.The company has obtained approval for the Krishna Defence and Allied Industries Limited Stock Option Scheme 1 ("ESOP 1") for 3,00,000 stock options from the Board of Directors through a resolution passed in the Board Meeting held on 5th July 2024. Subsequently, the ESOP 1 scheme was further approved by a &lt;BR&gt; 
special resolution passed in the Annual General Meeting held on 13th August 2024. Additionally, the scheme received in-principle approval from the National Stock Exchange (NSE) as on 17th October 2024. Further, the company granted 63,356 Stock Option to its employees by virtue of grant letter dated 11th, November, 2024. However, employees have accepted the 58,764 stock option at the vesting conditions which are outlined in their grant letter. The option outstading as on 30th September, 2025 is 57,448 options. Necessary impact have been considered. Further, the company has not yet granted the 2,36,644 Stock &lt;BR&gt; 
Option to its employees. The options are exercisable at an exercise price of Rs. 304 per share (Face Value of Rs.10 per share). Total expenses arising from sharebased payment transactions recognized in profit or loss as part of employee benefit expense is Rs. 75.30 lakhs for the half year ended on 30th Septemeber,2025 &lt;BR&gt; 
8.The statement of standalone financial results includes the result for the half year ended March 31, 2025, being the balancing figures between the audited &lt;BR&gt; 
